== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Gjall|Aggressive creature strategies#Gjall}}

=== Spit ===
Inhales a little before spitting out two balls of fire which inflict the [[Burning]] status (50 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] and 80 [[Damage types#Fire|Fire]] damage). Each fireball travels at 15 meters per second for up to 10 seconds before despawning and has a spread of 10–20 degrees. This attack can be used every 6 seconds when within 6–30 meters of a player — standing on top of the Gjall disables this attack.

=== Egg ===
Leans back and drops three eggs, which hatch into [[Tick]]s when hitting the ground. The hatched ticks do not carry the star tier of the Gjall — they will be 0 star. This ability can be used every 50 seconds when within 10–20 meters of a player — standing on top of the Gjall disables this ability.

=== Shake ===
Sways from side to side, hitting in a 3.41-meter radius sphere around themselves three times (20 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]] damage each hit). Gjalls can do this every 10 seconds when within 6 meters of a player. The attack cannot be blocked or dodged.

== Notes==
*Gjall are very dangerous creatures but can easily be outrun. Therefore, fleeing is an option if you have sufficient stamina.
*Pierce resistance is useful against the ticks if they become a problem

== Trivia ==
*In Norse mythology, the [[wikipedia:Gjallarhorn|Gjallarhorn]] is blown by Heimdallr to signal the commencement of Ragnarok.
*There are different ways to pronounce Gjall:
**In Old Norse, it would be pronounced /ˈɡjɑlː/ g'yall with hard g as in get and long l at the end. This pronunciation would be the closest to the Viking lore.
**In modern Norwegian, it is pronounced /jɑl/ yal, like [[wiktionary:y'all|y'all]]. Many players prefer this pronunciation and it also matches the puns in Gjall [[events]] better.
**In modern Swedish, it is pronounced /jalː/ yahll with a as in the first half of cow and long l at the end.
**In modern Danish, it is pronounced /ˈkjæl/ k'yael with k as in scar and ae in bat.
**In modern Icelandic, it is pronounced /catl/ tyahtl with ty as in stew.
*The name "Gjall" is probably inspired by the name of the mythological river Gjöll, meaning "noisy" "loud" or "scream".
*The sound made by the Gjall is most likely a reference to the sound made by the tripods in [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jzY099ihULs War of the Worlds]. It may also take inspiration from the World War 2-era German dive bomber [[wikipedia:Junkers Ju 87|Junkers JU-87 "Stuka"]] which was known for its loud siren as it approached high speeds on a bombing run. 
*The process behind the unique sounds made by Gjall was broken down in the video ''[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UwwLCM7Kzyc&ab_channel=IronGate What's up Gjall?]'' by Iron Gate.

